## Attempted real synthesis — blocked on account credit, not a code defect

$ curl -s -X POST "https://api.fish.audio/v1/tts" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $FISH_API_KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -H "model: s2.1-pro" \
    -d '{"text":"Zdravo! Ja sam Vitana, tvoj lični asistent za zdravlje i dugovečnost. Kako mogu danas da ti pomognem?","reference_id":"2ad62aaf885e4a14add09fe4a38ffd23","format":"mp3","normalize":true,"latency":"normal"}' \
    -o vitana_greeting_sr.mp3 -w "HTTP_STATUS:%{http_code}  SIZE:%{size_download} bytes\n"
HTTP_STATUS:402  SIZE:202 bytes
$ cat vitana_greeting_sr.mp3
{"status":402,"message":"Insufficient API credit. API credit is managed
independently from platform credit. Please visit
https://fish.audio/app/developers to view your API credit balance or add
funds."}
(the supplied FISH_API_KEY has no funded API credit — this is an account
state, not a bug in the request; the request shape itself is correct per
Fish's own published API docs, cross-checked at
docs.fish.audio/api-reference/endpoint/openapi-v1/text-to-speech)

